Module pellam "The Liberty of the Ice" {
  // ── The morning after ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Before first light on the morning after the ice goes, what became of each of the Fair's people is told as the
  // city's news, whatever became of the hired. In a world that goes on, the city goes on from it.
  Query newsHour() means thawed(lisk) and thirdDay() and hour(clock) == 5 and inPellam().
  Rule news_bel when newsHour() and goslingWedsBel(gosling) once says "Of the alderman and the gin-woman: Hamnet Gosling and Isabel Ashby carried the Frozen Lamb's sign up Swan Stairs together at nine last night, between them, and hung it over the door of a house in the Cheaping, and have not been seen since. The wedding was landed at the Landing, the clerk says, at the very end, by the alderman himself, who shouted it." { }
  Rule news_thessaly when newsHour() and thessalyWedsNoll(thessaly) once says "Of the printer and the factor's daughter: Noll Brisket carried his press up Hay Stairs on a sledge at dusk, with his wife pushing, and has set it up in a cellar in Bankside, where the first thing it printed this morning was the Frost Gazette, signed for the first time with a name: T. BRISKET." { }
  Rule news_gosling_harker when newsHour() and goslingHarker(gosling) once says "Of the wedding: Alderman Gosling and his bride went home to Fleece Row after the Landing, and at midnight, they say, when the ice went, the alderman was seen alone on the bridge in his chain, looking down at it." { }
  Rule news_callow_free when newsHour() and callowAcquitted(callow) once says "Of the heretic: Magister Callow, discharged, slept the night at the Spotted Calf, and this morning was found in the taproom arguing with Nab Pollard that a promise binds only what a man knew, and that this was what he had meant all along." { }
  Rule news_callow_stocks when newsHour() and callowConvicted(callow) and not callowDead(callow) once says "Of the heretic: Magister Callow sat in the stocks till the crier's call, preaching, and walked off the ice on two watermen's arms, and stood on Swan Stairs to watch it go out, laughing until he coughed. 'There,' he said. 'Did I not tell you?'" { }
  Rule news_callow_slipped when newsHour() and callowSlipped(callow) once says "Of the heretic: Magister Callow, who left his hand to answer for him, was seen last on the Black Reach in the second night, preaching to the river. Nobody has seen him since. The watermen say the Lisk Wife took him. The watermen say a great many things." { }
  Rule news_gant_clink when newsHour() and gantSafe(gant) once says "Of the debtor: Sir Lionel Gant has been elected, by the debtors of the Clink, master of the Clink yard, an honour he accepted in a speech of forty minutes." { }
  Rule news_gant_free when newsHour() and gantFree(gant) once says "Of the debtor: Sir Lionel Gant walked up Swan Stairs at nine last night, a free man, owing nobody anything, and was seen at midnight on the bridge in his shirt-sleeves in the frost, cheering the ice." { }
  Rule news_gant_taken when newsHour() and gantTaken(gant) once says "Of the debtor: Sir Lionel Gant is in the Fleece Row compter for thirty coin, saying to anyone who visits him that it was three." { }
  Rule news_bear_dead when newsHour() and bearDead(absolute) once says "Of the bear: Hester Mabb sat all day at the bear-stake with the broken chain in her lap, and went up the North Road this morning alone." { }
  Rule news_bear_live when newsHour() and bearCalmed(absolute) and not bearDead(absolute) once says "Of the bear: Hester Mabb walked Absolute off the ice at dusk, the last of the Fair's beasts, and up the North Road toward the woods, with the chain hanging slack between them." { }
  Rule news_quarle_cream when newsHour() and quarleCream(quarle) once says "Of the Frost Company: Mr. Quarle has taken a shop in the Cheaping, QUARLE'S FROST-CREAMS, and means to keep an ice-house of river ice cut by the watermen, so that there shall be frost-cream in Pellam in August. It is, he says, a perpetual frost of a kind." { }
  Rule news_quarle_ruined when newsHour() and quarleRuined(quarle) once says "Of the Frost Company: Mr. Quarle's tub went out with the ice, and Mr. Quarle with nothing in his pockets but the secret of the third salt, which he has offered to anyone at the Exchange for a coin." { }
  Rule news_saffery when newsHour() and not safferyTaken(saffery) and (hiredFled(lisk) or hiredReleased(lisk)) once says "Of the Lisk Wife: Widow Saffery stood on the bridge all the time the ice was going out, with her lantern, and when it had gone, blew it out, and went in." { }
  Rule news_dickon when newsHour() and urselMet(dickon) and dickonGone(dickon) and not drownedMetWolves(lisk) and not travelsWith(ursel, party) once says "Of the Cobbs: a woman in a caped coat and a big soft-spoken man with a cough were seen going up the North Road together in the thaw before light, arguing." { }
  Rule news_handfast when newsHour() and handfastLanded(party) once says "Of yourself: you are married, landed, from here to the sea. Ursel Cobb has told four people already, and lied about it to three." { }
  Rule news_ursel_gone when newsHour() and urselGone(ursel) once says "Of Ursel Cobb: nothing. Nobody has seen her since the Glove Post. Which is, you suppose, how she would want it told." { }
}
